WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.810
- Speaking of lawyers
being sanctioned in court,

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.210
we have a small update in
one of the Kraken lawsuits

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.043
in Michigan.

00:00:05.043 --> 00:00:06.899
In the King V. Whitmer suit in Michigan,

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:10.280
U.S. District Judge Parker
has a word for the attorneys.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.840
Specifically an order that states,

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.000
each attorney whose name
appears on any of Plaintiff's

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.830
pleadings or briefs shall be present

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.026
at the motion hearing
set for July 6th, 2021.

00:00:18.026 --> 00:00:20.500
And that hearing specifically
relates to three different

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.370
requests for sanctions
against Sidney Powell

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.740
and the whole Kraken team.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.579
And that's an order from a
judge that is not a happy judge.

00:00:26.579 --> 00:00:28.040
That is not an order that says,

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.640
everyone is going to get out fine.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.790
Now, we'll see what actually happens.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.510
Even when sanctions are issued,

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.200
often they're slaps on the wrist,

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.470
but this is not a happy judge.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.960
And we will see everyone
whose name appears

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.103
on any of plaintiff's briefs in court.

